9;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.298039);vertical-align:top;text-align:right;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(238,238,238);border-right-width:1px\"></td><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding-right:10px;padding-left:10px;vertical-align:top;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre;overflow:visible;word-wrap:normal\">  )\r\n</td></tr></tbody></table><br></div><div>If you un-comment line 74 and comment out line 75 (thus switching from HTML() to includeHTML()), then the slider inputs become numeric nuts, parts of the graphs are missing, and other computations go awry.</div><div><br></div><div>The JavaScript error console indicates a CSS problem involving local host, but the associated script is too long to post here.</div><div><br></div><div>about.html was generated from R Markdown.  I have tried several such generated files, including ones that are blank except for the default yaml front matter, but I get the same problem.  On the other hand includeHTML() works fine when the file is very simple (say, just the text &quot;TODO&quot;).</div><div><br></div><div>Has anyone encountered such a phenomenon?  I would not like to write the HTML file by hand.</div><div><br></div><div>Homer</div></div>"
